---
import PostLayout from '../../layouts/PostLayout.astro';
---

<PostLayout
  pageTitle="Bangkok Airwaves | Expedition"
  heroTitle="Bangkok<br>Airwaves"
  heroSubtitle="Glimpses of Thailand 2018"
  heroStyle="background-image:url('/assets/images/hero-placeholder.jpg')"
  date="MARCH 24TH, 2019"
  location="Bangkok, Thailand"
  locationLabel="Composition"
  footnote="&copy; ZUBINDOTCO"
  moreTitle="More in Travel"
>
  <Fragment slot="nav-left">WHAT'S NEW &#128293;</Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="nav-right">
    <div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;">
      <div class="nav-icons">
        <a class="nav-icon" href="#" aria-label="Search">&#8981;</a>
        <a class="nav-icon" href="#" aria-label="Grid">&#9783;</a>
        <a class="nav-icon" href="#" aria-label="Favourite">&#9825;</a>
      </div>
      <a class="edit-btn" href="#">&#9998; EDIT STORY</a>
    </div>
  </Fragment>

  <!-- INTRO TEXT -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="text">
      <p class="lede">
        A transit arrival by more than 50 flights a day, getting to our destination from Phuket was no
        challenge. A full-take a good part of the opening hours to explore to our hearts' content the heart of
        Bangkok Old Town area, in the between adjacent 8-odd temples.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION: HIGHLIGHTS -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title">Highlights</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        With only an afternoon to sample the best of Bangkok, we immediately set out for the Phra Nakhon
        District area &mdash; an incredibly historic part of Thailand's largest city and no surprise either. Here, in bold shades of red and
        lacquer, dozens of old temples, each with a unique characteristic &mdash; from temples displaying relics which
        formed a reputation from the entire world.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2-UP GRID -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Temple detail, Wat Pho"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Temple detail, Phra Nakhon district"></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>
        Located on Rattanakosin Island, south of the Grand Palace, stands the Wat Pho temple &mdash; home to a 46-metre-long
        gilded Buddhist reclining figure, the temple's greatest, most treasured artwork.
      </figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FULL-BLEED IMAGE -->
  <section class="full-bleed">
    <figure>
      <div class="media ph" data-label="Wat Arun panorama, Temple of the Dawn"></div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- TEXT -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        On the 'Thonburi' west bank of the Chao Phraya river lies <em>Wat Arun</em>, or the <strong>Temple of the Dawn</strong>.
        It's one of the many sites in Thailand where the neighbouring influence of intermingling Asian cultures is
        most evident. To an outside observer, it's a distinctly <strong>Khmer</strong> tower, a Hindu deity worshipped extensively in
        India, powered by <em>the radiance of the sun</em>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 3-UP GRID -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-3">
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Temple scene, Buddhist stupas"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Carved stone statues, Phra Nakhon"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Iconic temple facade, Phra Nakhon district"></div>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <div class="text" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <figcaption>
        Buddhist structures in the Phra Nakhon district, from ancient stupas, painted and carved stone statues and ornaments.
        On the right, we see the iconic faces of the most cherished temple.
      </figcaption>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- 2+1 GRID -->
  <section class="space-md">
    <div class="grid grid-2plus1">
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Farmers and stupas, Bangkok"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <div class="media ph" data-label="40-50m statues, Phra Nakhon district"></div>
      </figure>
      <figure class="span-2">
        <div class="media ph" data-label="Wide panorama, Bangkok Old Town temples"></div>
        <figcaption>
          Snapshots capturing some of the whiskful farmers surrounded simply by stupas or statues ranging from 40-50 meters in
          height. On our return, a lot of fun things.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- COVER QUOTE -->
  <section class="cover-quote">
    <div class="cover-ph" style="background:linear-gradient(135deg, #1a2c1a 0%, #0e1a0e 100%)"></div>
    <div class="inner">
      <figure>
        <figcaption>A majestic view of the temple's towering central stupa.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION TITLE: HIGHLIGHTS CONTINUED -->
  <section class="space-lg">
    <div class="text">
      <h2 class="section-title-center">Highlights</h2>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MORE TEXT -->
  <section class="space-sm">
    <div class="text">
      <p>
        A short cut and a definitive &mdash; to long-planned good times with good friends &mdash; To Beaches&hellip;
        Diving, Curry and Mekhong, Presto!
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- MORE CARDS -->
  <Fragment slot="more-cards">
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/innsbruck/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Into the Alps: Innsbruck</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Read</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Altstadt, Nordkette, and Castle Ambras</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/salzburg/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Into the Alps: Salzburg</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Read</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Untersberg, Hohensalzburg, Sound of Music</p>
    </a>
    <a class="more-card" href="/expeditions/verona/">
      <div class="more-thumb"></div>
      <p class="more-card-title">Verona</p>
      <span class="more-card-badge">Read</span>
      <p class="more-card-sub">Of Bridges and Brawls</p>
    </a>
  </Fragment>
</PostLayout>
